        <h2 id="armor-progression">Armor Progression</h2>
        <div class="guide-grid">
          <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="card-label">Profile</span>
            <h3>Normal Profiles</h3>
            <div style="text-align: center;"><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Sundial.png?45746" alt="Sundial"></div>
            <p>Purchase a <strong>Sundial (TOP PRIORITY)</strong> on the <strong>Auction House</strong></p>
            <p>As it lets you to throw away Rancher’s Boots(Nobody on normal profile uses this anyways), using the 4/4 Farming sets instead of 3/4, you get more profits</p>
            <p>After the Sundial, start up with the Farming Sets (Use 3/4 if you don’t have Sundial yet but craft the full set)</p>
            
          </div>

          <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="card-label">Profile</span>
            <h3>Ironman</h3>
            <p>Good Luck on doing Greenhouses, which will be explained later.</p>
            <p>Stick to Rancher’s Boots before even getting this.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="card-label">Comparison</span>
            <h3>For Both Profiles</h3>
            <p>The progress armor will be:</p>
            <h3>Farmhand Armor → Haymaker → Sprout → Tater → Cropie → Squash → Fermento → Helianthus</h3>
            <h3>Note that every sucessor armor requires the predecessor tier of armor to craft.</h3>
            
            <div style="text-align: center;">
              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Farmhand_Armor.png?00d20" alt="Farmhand Armor">
              <p>Farmhand Armor requires <strong>Farming 3</strong> to be used, in order to craft it, you need <strong>Wheat Collection 2</strong> to craft.
                It requires <strong>196 Wheat</strong> to craft. (40 for Helmet, 64 for Chestplate, 56 for Leggings, 36 for Boots)</p>
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Haymaker_Armor.png?78fd3" alt="Haymaker Armor">
              <p>Haymaker Armor requires <strong>Farming X(10)</strong> to be used, in order to craft it, you need <strong>Wheat Collection 6</strong> to craft.
                It requires <strong>32 Enchanted Wheat</strong> to craft. (8 each for each pieces)</p>
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Sprout_Armor.png?02e93" alt="Sprout Armor">
              <p>Sprout Armor requires <strong>Farming (Yet to know)</strong> to be used, in order to craft it, you need <strong>Carrot Collection 7</strong> to craft.
                It requires <strong>256 Enchanted Carrots</strong> to craft. (64 each for each piece)</p>
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Tater_Armor.png?1beeb" alt="Tater Armor">
              <p>Tater Armor requires <strong>Farming 20</strong> to be used, in order to craft it. It requires <strong>1024 Enchanted Potato</strong> to craft (256 each for each piece)</p>
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Cropie_Armor.png?cce21" alt="Cropie Armor">
              <p>After obtaining Tater Set, you can farm <strong>Wheat, Carrot, Potato</strong> any 1 of them with a 0.05% chance of to drop a Cropie, and the Cropie Talisman. 
                You’ll need <strong>80 Cropies, 40 Enchanted Hay Bale, 18 Box of Seeds, 45 Enchanted Baked Potato, 30 Enchanted Golden Carrot</strong> for the whole 4/4 set, 
                256 Cropies for the Cropie Talisman.</p>
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Squash_Armor.png?f4ca1" alt="Squash Armor">
              <p>After getting the Cropie set, farming Pumpkin, Melon, and Cocoa Beans have a 0.03% chance of dropping Squash while wearing 4/4 of the set. 
                It requires <strong>80 Squashes, 36 Polished Pumpkins, 144 Enchanted Melon Blocks, 50 Enchanted Cookie</strong> to craft from Cropie.</p>
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Fermento_Armor.png?d0625" alt="Fermento Armor">
              <p>Squash, farming Sugar Cane, Cactus, Mushroom and Nether Warts will drop Fermento, with a 0.007% chance of dropping when wearing 4/4 of the set. 
                It requires 8 Condensed Fermento(1 Condensed is crafted by using 9 Fermentos), 96 Enchanted Sugar Cane, 64 of each Enchanted Mushroom Block, 70 Mutated Nether Warts and 25 Enchanted Cactus to craft.</p> 
              <br>

              <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Helianthus_Armor.png?e39f2" alt="Helianthus Armor">
              <p>You are now on the Last Tier of the armor, Helianthus, by farming Sunflowers (Set your Garden time to Day), Moonflowers (Set your Garden time to Night), Wild Roses, with a 0.004% chance of dropping a Helianthus. 
                It also requires 8 Condensed Helianthus (1 Condensed is crafted by using 9 Helianthus), 3 Stacks of Compacted Wild Rose, 4 Stacks of Compacted Sunflower and Moonflower to craft.</p>
              <br>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="pets-equipment">Pets &amp; Equipment</h2>
        <p>
          <h2>Pets</h2>
          <h3>General Farming(Normal Farming when breaking Crops)</h3>
          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Rose_Dragon_Pet.png?8095f" alt="Rose Dragon"></p>
            <p><strong>Rose Dragon</strong>being the <strong>BiS</strong> Pet as it provides a large amount of <strong><span class="farming-fortune-label">FF</span>(Like a single pet with 250<span class="farming-fortune-label">FF</span> without any buffs, with every Farming Pet Maxed)</strong></p>

            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Elephant_Pet.png?37719&20260426121230" alt="Elephant Pet"></p>
            <p><strong>Elephant</strong> for overall more <strong><span class="farming-fortune-label">FF</span></strong>, when reaching <strong>Mythic</strong> provided <strong>+20% Sowdust</strong> on Farming</p>

            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Mooshroom_Cow_Pet.png?48edd" alt="Mooshroom Cow Pet"></p>
            <p><strong>Mooshroom Cow</strong> for <i><strong>slightly</strong></i> better than <strong>Elephant</strong> and more coins due to the <strong>Mushroom</strong> drops</p>
          </div>
          
          <br>

          <h3>Pet Items</h3>
          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <p><img src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hypixel-skyblock/images/1/1d/Green_Bandana.png/revision/latest?cb=20230328150836" alt="Green Bandana"></p>
            <p><strong>Green Bandana</strong> for more <span class="farming-fortune-label">FF</span></p>

            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Enchanted_Lily_Pad.png?bfd63" alt="Lucky Clover"></p>
            <p><strong>Lucky Clover</strong> for <strong><span class="overbloom-label">+7 OB</span></strong> making an alternative replacement before getting a <strong>Poignant Lucky Clover</strong></p>

            <p><img src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hypixel-skyblock/images/f/fb/Enchanted_Big_Dripleaf.png/revision/latest?cb=20260331230609" alt="Poignant Lucky Clover"></p>
            <p><strong>Poignant Lucky Clover</strong> for the <strong><span class="overbloom-label">+13 OB</span></strong>, making it the <strong>BiS</strong> Pet Item for Farming and Killing Pests</p>
          </div>

          <br><br>

          <h3>Killing Pests</h3>
          <p>If you had <strong>Rose Dragon Pet</strong>, skip through this. Just use <strong>Rose Dragon</strong> for <strong>both</strong>.</p>
          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Hedgehog_Pet.png?ce0f3" alt="Hedgehog Pet"></p>
            <p>Otherwise, a <strong>Hedgehog Pet</strong> with the same Pet Item as <strong>General Farming</strong> suggested above, a good alternative for new players without having the coins
              for a <strong>Rose Dragon.</strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <br><br>

          <h3>Pest Farming(When spawning Pests)</h3>
          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Mosquito.png?5df54" alt="Mosquito"></p>
            <p><strong>Mosquito Pet</strong> being the <strong>BiS</strong> for Pest spawning, <strong>any Rarity</strong> of it would work</p>
          </div>


          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Slug.png?5a1ec" alt="Legendary Slug" style="display: block; margin: 0 auto;">
            <p style="margin-top: 4px;"><strong>Legendary Slug Pet</strong> as an alternative for <strong>Mosquito Pet</strong> due to cheap price (Common Mosquito is 120m+)</p>
          </div>

          <br>

          <h3>Pet Items</h3>
          <div style="text-align: center;">
            <p><img src="https://hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki/images/Brown_Bandana.png?3b5f5" alt="Brown Bandana"></p>
            <p><strong>Brown Bandana, The one and the only</strong> Pet Item for Pest Spawning</p>
          </div>
        </p>

